+"""Vendored copy of beets' bundled `replaygain` plugin, patched to fix
+`MetaflacBackend` writing ReplayGain tags to files before they've been
+copied to their final library location.
+
+`metaflac --add-replay-gain` computes and writes tags in one step -- there
+is no read-only mode -- so calling it against `item.filepath` mutates
+whatever the file's current path happens to be. Every other backend here
+only measures in memory and lets the plugin's own `write` flag decide if
+and when to persist, deferring the actual write until after the file has
+been copied/moved (see the `import_stages` vs `manipulate_files` ordering
+in beets' importer). `MetaflacBackend` broke that contract, so on a fresh
+`auto` import it would write ReplayGain tags straight onto files still
+sitting in the *source*/staging directory, before the copy step ever ran.
+
+Fixed by switching to `metaflac --scan-replay-gain` (added in a metaflac
+release newer than what beets currently assumes), which reports the same
+computed values on stdout without writing anything -- verified to produce
+numerically identical gain/peak values to `--add-replay-gain`, just without
+the side effect. See `MetaflacBackend._scan`.
+
+This is a stopgap until the fix lands upstream in beets itself; delete
+this file (and the matching Dockerfile COPY line) once it does.
+
+Upstream source: https://github.com/beetbox/beets/blob/master/beetsplug/replaygain.py
+"""
+
 from __future__ import annotations
 
